# Design System & Accessibility

## Tokens
- Use only design tokens (color, spacing, radius, typography, elevation, motion) from the project's token source. No raw hex values, magic pixel numbers, or ad-hoc font sizes in components.
- If a needed token does not exist, add it to the token source first, then use it.
- Prefer semantic tokens (`color.text.primary`, `space.4`) over raw palette values.
- Support light and dark themes through tokens, not per-component overrides.

## WCAG 2.2 AA (minimums)
- Text contrast >= 4.5:1 (>= 3:1 for large text and for UI component boundaries/icons).
- Every interactive element is keyboard reachable, has a visible focus indicator, and a logical focus order.
- Touch/click targets >= 44x44 pt (iOS/web) or 48x48 dp (Android).
- Inputs have programmatic labels; errors are announced and not conveyed by color alone.
- Images have alt text (or are marked decorative); icons-only buttons have accessible names.
- Respect reduced-motion and text-scaling settings. No layout that breaks at 200% zoom.
- Use semantic elements/roles (`button`, `nav`, `main`, headings in order) before reaching for ARIA.

## Components
- Small, composable, single-purpose. Variants and sizes are props mapped to tokens, not copy-pasted styles.
- Every component handles loading, empty, error, and disabled states.
- Presentational components do not fetch data or know about the backend.
- Reuse existing components from the design system before creating new ones.
